---
import Studio from "@/layouts/Studio.astro";
---

<Studio
	title="Privacy Policy · Learn Gita (Android)"
	description="Privacy policy for Learn Gita, the offline daily Bhagavad Gita app for Android. We collect no data."
>
	<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-14 space-y-10">
		<section class="space-y-4">
			<div class="flex items-center gap-3">
				<img src="/prasuco-wordmark.png" alt="Prasuco" class="h-7 w-auto" />
				<p class="text-sm text-muted">Prasuco · Learn Gita for Android</p>
			</div>
			<h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">
				Privacy Policy
			</h1>
			<p class="text-[15px] text-muted leading-relaxed">
				Learn Gita is an offline daily Bhagavad Gita reader. This policy
				explains what the app does with your information. Short version:
				it collects nothing and sends nothing anywhere.
			</p>
			<p class="text-sm text-muted">Effective 11 October 2026.</p>
		</section>

		<hr class="border-border" />

		<section class="space-y-3">
			<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Data collection</h2>
			<p class="text-[15px] text-muted leading-relaxed">
				Learn Gita collects no personal data. It has no accounts, no
				analytics, no advertising SDKs, no crash reporters, and makes no
				network requests of any kind. There is nothing transmitted off
				your device, because there is nothing to transmit.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="space-y-3">
			<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Data stored on your device</h2>
			<p class="text-[15px] text-muted leading-relaxed">
				Everything the app remembers lives only in its private on-device
				storage:
			</p>
			<ul class="text-[15px] text-muted leading-relaxed list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
				<li>verses marked as read and your day streak,</li>
				<li>bookmarked verses and private notes,</li>
				<li>settings such as reminder time and translation choice,</li>
				<li>the bundled Gita text itself, copied into a local database on first launch.</li>
			</ul>
			<p class="text-[15px] text-muted leading-relaxed">
				Uninstalling the app deletes all of it. Clearing app data does
				the same.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="space-y-3">
			<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Permissions used</h2>
			<ul class="text-[15px] text-muted leading-relaxed list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
				<li>
					Notifications: one optional morning reminder with the daily
					verse. You choose the time during onboarding and can turn it
					off at any point.
				</li>
				<li>
					Run at startup: only to re-schedule that same reminder and
					refresh the home-screen widget after a reboot.
				</li>
				<li>
					Photos and media: only when you tap Save image, to store a
					verse card you asked for in your gallery.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="space-y-3">
			<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Children</h2>
			<p class="text-[15px] text-muted leading-relaxed">
				The app is usable by all ages and collects no data from anyone,
				children included.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="space-y-3">
			<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Changes to this policy</h2>
			<p class="text-[15px] text-muted leading-relaxed">
				If the app ever starts handling data differently, this page will
				be updated before any release that includes the change.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="space-y-3">
			<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Contact</h2>
			<p class="text-[15px] text-muted leading-relaxed">
				Questions about privacy in Learn Gita: open an issue at{" "}
				<a
					href="https://github.com/prasuco/learn-gita/issues"
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener noreferrer"
					class="text-brand hover:underline"
				>
					github.com/prasuco/learn-gita
				</a>
				.
			</p>
		</section>
	</div>
</Studio>
